  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 749 AM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nThe current pattern will shift east through the long term\nperiod. The upper ridge will shift into the area through the\nweekend as a weak shortwave moves southeast of the area on\nSunday. Look for the ridge to remain over the central CONUS\nthrough the middle of next week before SW flow returns as\nensemble guidance and tools show troughing becoming established\nover the western CONUS. \n\nOverall, the pattern will favor a warming trend, with Sunday\nstarting having lows in the 20s/30s and highs in the 50s,\nincreasing to lows in the 40s/50s and highs in the 60s to low\n70s for the middle to end of next week.\n\nPrecip chances: The Sunday shortwave could bring some light rain\nto the area as it moves southwest of us. The track of the\nshortwave and very dry airmass over the area will not favor our\narea to receive rainfall. Current forecast features 10-20%\nchance of rain over the far SW CWA, basically along the KS/OK \nand MO/OK borders. This is backed up well by the NBM probability\nof >= 0.01 inches of QPF being 15-25% over that area. \n\nOtherwise, the rest of the forecast features minimal rain\nchances. We will see some 15-30% chance for rain enter the\npicture late next week in the more active SW flow pattern, but\npredictability of any shortwave tracks and resulting rain \nchances is very low at that time frame.",
